<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cesena</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cesena is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romagna">Romagna</a>, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, on the Savio river near the Adriatic. Ruled at times by the Ordelaffi and the Malatesta, it was the seat of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cesare-borgia">Cesare Borgia</a>'s government as Duke of Romagna in 1501–1503. It is known for the Malatestiana Library, founded by Domenico Malatesta Novello in the mid-15th century, one of the first public libraries in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cesena.jpg" alt="Cesena" width="320" height="174" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Uomodis08 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Panorama_di_Cesena_e_le_sue_colline.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
